THEOREM (to verify): TNC HOLDS for BINOMIAL R = r0 + rd u^d (d=M+N).
  Lambda = r0 u^{-N} + rd u^{M}, charges {-N, M} ONLY.  CT(Lambda^m) = sum over
  a+b=m with -Na+Mb=0.  Minimal solution a=M/g, b=N/g (g=gcd(M,N)), m0=(M+N)/g,
  and CT(m0) = C(m0, M/g) r0^{M/g} rd^{N/g} -- a SINGLE term, no cancellation, != 0.
  So a binomial is NEVER a nullcone element => TNC holds at every bidegree for 2-term R.

